              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2024-45336?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.22.11",
              "help": {
                "text": "The HTTP client drops sensitive headers after following a cross-domain redirect. For example, a request to a.com/ containing an Authorization header which is redirected to b.com/ will not send that header to b.com.\n\nIn the event that the client received a subsequent same-domain redirect, however, the sensitive headers would be restored. For example, a chain of redirects from a.com/, to b.com/1, and finally to b.com/2 would incorrectly send the Authorization header to b.com/2.\n",
                "markdown": "> The HTTP client drops sensitive headers after following a cross-domain redirect. For example, a request to a.com/ containing an Authorization header which is redirected to b.com/ will not send that header to b.com.\n\nIn the event that the client received a subsequent same-domain redirect, however, the sensitive headers would be restored. For example, a chain of redirects from a.com/, to b.com/1, and finally to b.com/2 would incorrectly send the Authorization header to b.com/2.\n\n|                                        |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.17  |\n|Affected range  <1.22.11                |\n|Fixed version   1.22.11                 |\n"
              },
